  "live_records": {
    "q-38819": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38819",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=4My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 4My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
