    "q-163576": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163576",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(8-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
